    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-3)^2=9$; $-3^2=-9$. Brackets make $-3$ the base in the first expression. In the second, square $3$ before applying the minus sign.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(-3)^2&=(-3)\\times(-3)\\\\&=9\\\\-3^2&=-(3\\times3)\\\\&=-9\\end{align*}$$\nBrackets make the negative number the base, so both factors are negative. Without brackets, the index applies to $3$ and the minus sign is applied afterwards.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
